      {
        "text": "AgentCascade is a production-oriented multi-agent framework designed for building robust, scalable, and controllable LLM applications. Originally forked from Qwen-Agent, it has evolved into an independent system with a focus on orchestration, security, and developer productivity.",
        "token": 51
      },
      {
        "text": "Core Features",
        "token": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "🤖 Multi-Agent Orchestration",
        "token": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "OrchestratorAgent (agent_orchestrator.py): A supervisor agent that manages sub-agent lifecycles, intercepts call_agent/dismiss_agent tool calls, and handles multi-agent streaming as a unified generator.",
        "token": 44
      },
      {
        "text": "AgentPool (agent_pool.py): Centralized agent management with per-instance conversation persistence (JSONL), context compression (auto + manual modes), and real-time state synchronization.",
        "token": 34
      },
      {
        "text": "🛡️ Production Safety & Control",
        "token": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "OperationManager (operation_manager.py): A mandatory approval system for all mutating operations (file edits, code execution, system commands). Every edit creates timestamped .bak backups automatically.",
        "token": 35
      },
      {
        "text": "Path Isolation: Strict workspace-relative path resolution ensures agents never access or expose host-absolute paths.",
        "token": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "Graceful Lifecycle: Comprehensive signal handling (SIGINT/SIGTERM) ensuring clean shutdowns, backup cleanup, and state preservation.",
        "token": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "💻 Modern Web UI & API",
        "token": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Custom Console (web_ui/): A lightweight, high-performance HTML/JS frontend replacing legacy Gradio interfaces. Supports multi-agent tab switching, approval workflows, and rich tool result rendering.",
        "token": 37
      },
      {
        "text": "WebSocket API Server (api_server.py): A headless backend allowing any external interface (Electron, VS Code extensions, CLI) to control the agent cluster.",
        "token": 32
      },
      {
        "text": "🛠️ Robust Tooling",
        "token": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "XML-Based Tool Protocols: Large text payloads (code, file contents) are handled via XML tags to eliminate JSON escaping corruptions.",
        "token": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "PythonExecutor Improvements: Hardened execution with proper exception isolation and batch crash recovery.",
        "token": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "Multi-Modal Support: Native handling of images and files within tool results, including backend proxying for local file rendering.",
        "token": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "News",
        "token": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "🔥🔥🔥Feb 16, 2026: Open-sourced Qwen3.5. For usage examples, refer to Qwen3.5 Agent Demo.",
        "token": 37
      },
      {
        "text": "Jan 27, 2026: Open-sourced agent evaluation benchmark DeepPlanning and added AgentCascade documentation.",
        "token": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "Sep 23, 2025: Added Qwen3-VL Tool-call Demo, supporting tools such as zoom in, image search, and web search.",
        "token": 35
      },
      {
        "text": "Jul 23, 2025: Add Qwen3-Coder Tool-call Demo; Added native API tool call interface support, such as using vLLM's built-in tool call parsing.",
        "token": 42
