      {
        "text": "Getting Started",
        "token": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Installation",
        "token": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Install from PyPI:",
        "token": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "pip install -U \"agent-cascade[rag,code_interpreter,mcp]\"",
        "token": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "Install from source for development:",
        "token": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "git clone https://github.com/LuckyKo/AgentCascade.git",
        "token": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "cd AgentCascade",
        "token": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "pip install -e ./\"[rag,code_interpreter,mcp]\"",
        "token": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Preparation: Model Service",
        "token": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "You can use Alibaba Cloud's DashScope, or deploy your own OpenAI-compatible API (vLLM, Ollama, etc.).",
        "token": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "Set DASHSCOPE_API_KEY environment variable if using DashScope.",
        "token": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "For local models, configure the model_server endpoint in your agent config.",
        "token": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "Developing Your Own Agent",
        "token": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "The following example shows how to create an agent with custom tools:",
        "token": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "from agent_cascade.agents import Assistant",
        "token": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "from agent_cascade.tools.base import BaseTool, register_tool",
        "token": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "@register_tool('my_image_gen')",
        "token": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "class MyImageGen(BaseTool):",
        "token": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "    description = 'AI painting service'",
        "token": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "    parameters = [{'name': 'prompt', 'type': 'string', 'required': True}]",
        "token": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "    def call(self, params: str, **kwargs) -> str:",
        "token": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "\t# Implementation...",
        "token": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "\treturn '{\"image_url\": \"...\"}'",
        "token": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "llm_cfg = {'model': 'qwen-max-latest'}",
        "token": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "bot = Assistant(llm=llm_cfg, function_list=['my_image_gen', 'code_interpreter'])",
        "token": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "# Run as chatbot",
        "token": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "for response in bot.run(messages=[{'role': 'user', 'content': 'draw a dog'}]):",
        "token": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "    print(response)",
        "token": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "FAQ",
        "token": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "How to use Code Interpreter?: Ensure Docker is running. The tool writes and executes code in an isolated container.",
        "token": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "How to use MCP?: Configure mcpServers in your agent config. See MCP Example.",
        "token": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "Does it support Parallel Tool Calls?: Yes, natively supported via the nous prompt template.",
        "token": 18
